// spec: a generic lambda names a static local of the function it is written in, and an instance (a template the lambda is passed to) calls it first, in a build of 64 modules (and the release suite's): the call operator, emitted where that instance is, reads and writes the one static the function does, whichever module each is in (`6 12 26 32 46 52 66 72 86 92 106 112`)
// factorio: none known; found reviewing streaming's pieces (step 4): a non-generic lambda's call operator is placed and owned as its writer's (emitCallOperatorOnDemand) and works at any module count
// pending: the operator is emitted with its first caller, an instance placed by its name's hash, and the static is `internal` in its writer's module: "use of undefined value '@"counted0()::calls.N"'", clang rejects that module (master at --modules 64 and 128, debug and release; 1 and 4 happened to share a module) (B)
// kppc: --modules 64
template<typename F> int apply(F f) { return f(2); }

// Each: the function's own update of its static, the operator's (through apply), then the sum of the
// two reads: the same object, so twice the value the operator left.
int counted0()
{
  static int calls = 0;
  calls = calls + 1;
  auto g = [](auto x) { calls = calls + x; return calls; };
  int seen = apply(g);
  return seen + calls;
}
